{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.96.8.a001", "note": "Imperative to *Ascribe*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.96.8.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.96.8.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.96.8.a002", "note": "Preposition to *unto*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.96.8.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.96.8.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.96.8.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.96.8.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.96.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.96.8.a004", "note": "Construct noun takes a supplied *the* under rule 29; no article morpheme stands in the chain.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.96.8.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.96.8.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.96.8.a005", "note": "The ASV recasts the construct relation with *unto*; under rule 19 the preposition belongs to the rectum, headed on the noun. Discontinuous around the possessive under rule 25. The supplied *due* is not the relation's rendering but a lexical predicate and is placed separately.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.96.8.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.96.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.96.8.a006", "note": "*due* is a supplied lexical adjective predicating something of the glory, exactly as *done* in `חֲמַס אֶרֶץ` → *violence done to the land* under rule 20's nominal-recasting boundary; a construct relation licenses the preposition *unto* but not a supplied lexical predicate. Competing reading: *due unto* whole on the rectum as the recast relation under rule 19; rejected because *due* names a state the Hebrew never writes. ASV italic corroborates without deciding (rule 7).", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.96.8.a007", "note": "Suffix to possessive under rule 18.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.96.8.006"], "s